  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering science, capacity development and cooperation for freshwater resources management in the Pacific SIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific region is among the most vulnerable regions to the impact of climate change with more frequent water-related extreme events. Sound science-based policies and international cooperation are essential for sustaining the freshwater resources and bolstering socio-economic development of the Pacific communities. The UNESCO IHP is uniquely placed to extend its expertise by consolidating and fostering alliances and scientific exchanges, and by encouraging knowledge sharing and operational partnerships for increasing water security. Activities will be supported to strengthen capacities of the Pacific SIDS in freshwater management, notably through re-engaging with the IHP programme in the Pacific and through advanced research, education, capacity building and cooperation among water experts, policy makers, communities and youth.</narrative>
  </description>
